From 2e2306c32542826fae07dd9380929e43f34acdec Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 03:03:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] FORK-29: mod-decided block use (server-events.block-used:
 default, pass, consume)

A server mod that asked for blocks decides, for a right click on one of its blocks, whether the block's own use runs (default),
is skipped so the held item is used against it (pass), or the click is taken (consume). Test mod: examples/block-use.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RYe92n7spgy8vtm4CovRWA
